            <ArticleTitle>Pediatric knee. Clinical assessment and common disorders.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1067-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Knee pain and injury are commonly seen in children and adolescents. A comprehensive evaluation of the knee is built on an appreciation of the anatomy, biomechanics, and pathophysiology of common disorders. This article considers these issues and describes a sequential technique for physical examination of the knee. Relevant imaging options and management strategies also are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
